{"repositoryId":917726903,"availability":"available","full":"aziddy/ClipboardPhotoEditor","name":"ClipboardPhotoEditor","description":"Paste (from your Clipboard) your Image into the Tab and then Edit (crop, resize, ....) and receive the newly edited Image in your Clipboard for use Elsewhere","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-01-16T14:36:13Z","updated":"2026-10-15T22:00:08Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://clipboard-photo-editor.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://clipboard-photo-editor.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:24.712Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:24.712Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:24.712Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T15:52:24.712Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Paste or import an image, edit it in one unified canvas, and copy or download the final composition.","The editor supports image and editable text layers, drawing, erasing, cropping, resizing, layer ordering, opacity, visibility, undo, redo, clipboard export, and PNG/JPEG downloads from a single workspace.","Added images initially fit inside the document while retaining their original pixels. Moving, scaling, rotating, and resizing the document preserve that detail. Brush and eraser edits use the layer's full resolution; cropping removes excluded pixels without downscaling the remaining image. Exports use the document's dimensions. Images can be up to 12,000 pixels on each side."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aziddy/ClipboardPhotoEditor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5dd97c2c726c40e5a5d070ed6efbbaafe0ea8379ee62c44efe6714c96f632333","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:24.833Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:24.833Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Paste or import an image, edit it in one unified canvas, and copy or download the final composition.","sourceUrl":"https